  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345178",
      "title": "Revisiting Operators",
      "sourceHash": "696c7f8623ad3b42927f0475ded24cc6669b6b0328e2440abb5f2fb2a696741c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 5.04,
          "en": "Select and const are super important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.04,
          "end": 8.79,
          "en": "Another very important concept related to values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.79,
          "end": 10.59,
          "en": "are operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.59,
          "end": 13.83,
          "en": "For example, in JavaScript we can perform math.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.83,
          "end": 17.55,
          "en": "We can use the plus, minus, times,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 20.7,
          "en": "and division operator to perform math,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.7,
          "end": 23.733,
          "en": "and to, for example, divide 10 by five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.78,
          "end": 27.03,
          "en": "And what's important to know about JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.03,
          "end": 30.3,
          "en": "is that the plus operator for adding things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.3,
          "end": 34.14,
          "en": "cannot just be used for numbers, as I'm doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.14,
          "end": 36.36,
          "en": "And the difference between numbers and strings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.36,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "is that they don't have quotes around them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 41.46,
          "en": "But instead it can also be used with text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.46,
          "end": 43.95,
          "en": "For example, \"hello\" plus \"world\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.95,
          "end": 48.18,
          "en": "for concatenating two strings into one longer string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 49.2,
          "en": "With that code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.2,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "we would get helloworld like this as one word,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 55.86,
          "en": "because I have no blank anywhere in these strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.86,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "But as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.79,
          "end": 59.46,
          "en": "the plus operator works absolutely fine here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "So you can also use it for concatenating strings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 66.78,
          "en": "Now, besides plus, minus, times and division,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.78,
          "end": 69.66,
          "en": "you also have some other crucial operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.66,
          "end": 72.75,
          "en": "For example, the triple equal sign operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.75,
          "end": 75.42,
          "en": "which is used for checking for equality.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.42,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "And this operator therefore yields a Boolean value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 84.11,
          "en": "In this case here, false, because 10 isn't equal to five.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.66,
          "end": 87.27,
          "en": "If I would be checking 10 equals 10,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.27,
          "end": 88.953,
          "en": "I instead would be getting true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.06,
          "end": 91.92,
          "en": "Now, besides checking for equality,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.92,
          "end": 95.00999999999999,
          "en": "you can also check for things being greater or smaller",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.00999999999999,
          "end": 96.24000000000001,
          "en": "than other things,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.24000000000001,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "or greater or equal or smaller or equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 103.86,
          "en": "And these comparison operators are also very commonly used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.86,
          "end": 104.85,
          "en": "in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.85,
          "end": 107.25,
          "en": "and will be used a lot in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.25,
          "end": 109.68,
          "en": "typically in conjunction with the if keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.68,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "and if statements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 114.84,
          "en": "which allows you to execute some code conditionally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 114.84,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "For example, here I'm comparing 10 to 10,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 120.06,
          "en": "which is kind of redundant of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.06,
          "end": 123.72,
          "en": "Typically you would instead compare some dynamic user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.72,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "But for this demo here, I'm using two hard coded values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 128.91,
          "en": "and if this condition is met,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.91,
          "end": 131.58,
          "en": "which in this case here will of course always be the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.58,
          "end": 134.13,
          "en": "the code in the if statement will execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.13,
          "end": 137.52,
          "en": "But I'll get back to if statements a little bit later again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.52,
          "end": 140.61,
          "en": "Here, if I reload this idea for get works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 140.61,
          "end": 143.04,
          "en": "because of course this condition here is always met.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.04,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "Again, this is a redundant condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.8,
          "en": "In this course, in the apps we're going to build with React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 148.8,
          "end": 151.263,
          "en": "you will see conditions that make more sense.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}